---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `scores <- [80, 95, 70]
best <- scores[1]

FOR EACH s IN scores
{
  IF(s > best)
  {
    best <- s
  }
}
DISPLAY(best)`;
const Q2 = `let x = prompt("Number: ");   // user types 5
console.log(x * 2);
console.log(x + 2);`;
const Q5 = `let n = 10;

while (n > 0) {
  console.log(n);
}`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 8</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Five questions &middot; 9 minutes &middot; cumulative
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>Ten minutes, five questions, <b>the whole quarter</b>. This one is shaped like the real thing: mixed notation, mixed topics, no warning about which is which. It is also your last practice before the checkpoint.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 9 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper; do not run
            the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank &mdash; the AP exam has no penalty for a
            wrong answer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <p>
            Four have exactly one correct answer. One asks you to select
            <i>all</i> that apply.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q1}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Question 1 — exam notation"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>80</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>95</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>70</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>245</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>What does this code display?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q2}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Question 2"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>10</code> then <code>7</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>10</code> then <code>52</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>52</code> then <code>52</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>10</code> then <code>10</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>Which statements about <code>DISPLAY</code> are true?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) It adds a space after the value it shows</li>
            <li>(B) It starts a new line after each call</li>
            <li>(C) Two consecutive calls produce output on one line</li>
            <li>(D) It is the exam-notation equivalent of <code>console.log</code></li>
            <li>(E) It can display the result of an expression</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>A robot faces <b>up</b> on an open grid. After <code>ROTATE_RIGHT()</code>, <code>ROTATE_RIGHT()</code>, <code>MOVE_FORWARD()</code>, which way has it moved?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Up one square</li>
            <li>(B) Down one square</li>
            <li>(C) Right one square</li>
            <li>(D) Left one square</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5</h3>

          <p>Which of these produces an infinite loop?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q5}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Question 5"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) It is not infinite; it runs ten times.</li>
            <li>(B) It is infinite because <code>n</code> never changes inside the loop.</li>
            <li>(C) It is infinite because <code>while</code> always repeats forever.</li>
            <li>(D) It is infinite because <code>n</code> starts above zero.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Five answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>2 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
